      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Noise & denoise playground\n\nThe photo is corrupted twice - zero-mean Gaussian noise (the 'Add Gaussian noise' subgraph: cv2.randn centered at 128, then image + noise - 128 so it can darken AND brighten in uint8) and salt & pepper (the 'Add salt & pepper' subgraph: a uniform field thresholded at both tails) - then handed to four denoisers. What to look for: the median filter erases salt & pepper outright but rounds corners; Gaussian blur just smears both noise and edges; bilateral keeps strong edges (it refuses to average across them); NL-means searches the whole window for similar patches and wins on texture, at 100x the cost. The labels are stamped per tile and the sheet is tiled with 'CV Stack Images'.\n\nThe displayed upper row is the result of using Canny edge detection over the below blured images without additional morphologic operations."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
